# Closing Checklist ([PROJECT_NAME])

Read when:

1. before final handoff,
2. when someone says run closeout,
3. when claiming the work is done,
4. when the operator asks whether everything required is actually complete.

Skip when:

1. the task is still actively blocked and only a status update is needed.

## Purpose

This is the explicit final closeout gate.

The agent must report `PASS`, `FAIL`, or `N/A` for each item before claiming done.

## Closing Gate

| Check | Result | Evidence / Note |
|---|---|---|
| User request answered | PASS / FAIL | |
| Scope stayed within request | PASS / FAIL | |
| Acceptance boundary checked | PASS / FAIL / N/A | |
| Project state updated | PASS / FAIL / N/A | `docs/PROJECT_STATE.md` |
| Session brief refreshed | PASS / N/A | `docs/SESSION_BRIEF.md` or routed-startup not used |
| Tests or commands run | PASS / FAIL / N/A | list commands and exit results |
| Verify gate run | PASS / FAIL / N/A | `scripts/verify.sh` or explicit rationale |
| Review decision recorded | PASS / N/A | `docs/REVIEW_CHECKLIST.md` or accepted review artifact |
| Traceability updated | PASS / N/A | Path IDs or rationale |
| Docs and changelog updated | PASS / N/A | files updated or reason skipped |
| UI-visible evidence checked | PASS / N/A | browser smoke, screenshot/trace, or manual click path |
| Data safety checked | PASS / N/A | snapshot/restore evidence or no data touched |
| Security/privacy risk checked | PASS / N/A | scan or review note |
| Operator dashboard updated | PASS / N/A | `docs/OPERATOR_DASHBOARD.md` for orchestrated work |
| Open risks listed | PASS / FAIL | risks or `None` |
| Remaining work listed | PASS / FAIL | follow-ups or `None` |

## Required Final Handoff Shape

After running the checklist, the handoff should say:

1. what changed,
2. what commands or tests ran and with what result,
3. closing checklist summary,
4. open risks or follow-ups,
5. whether the work is done, blocked, or waiting on operator action.

Do not claim done if any required item is `FAIL`.

## Update Rules

Update this file when:

1. handoff expectations change,
2. verify or review requirements change,
3. closeout evidence expectations change.